Part 1  T4-T1 on a generic FRW pair, and with a static source moving through it (own Christoffel code from metric jets)
====================================================================================================
  [PASS] (control) T4-T1 = 3 (B + 2 w q)^2 - 4 p^2 - 8 q^2 with B = (2 H nn - Hh (nn^2+rr^2))/nn: the cosmological (timelike) part is +3B^2 (positive), the static (spacelike) part -4p^2-8q^2 (negative), and the boost enters only as B -> B + 2 w q   (T = -(-12*H**2*nn**2 + 12*H*Hh*nn**3 + 12*H*Hh*nn*rr**2 - 24*H*nn**2*q*w - 3*Hh**2*nn**4 - 6*Hh**2*nn**2*rr**2 - 3*Hh**2*rr**4 + 12*Hh*nn**3*q*w + 12*Hh*nn*q*rr**2*w + 4*nn**2*p**2 - 12*nn**2*q**2*w**2 + 8*nn**2*q**2)/nn**2)
  [PASS] (control) static limit -4(p^2+2q^2) and FRW limit 3B^2 recovered; B = 0 on the symmetric branch (H = Hh, rr = nn = 1)
  => Q = -T/a0^2 = [4p^2 + 8q^2 - 3 (B + 2 w q)^2]/a0^2: a cosmological relative expansion enters the local argument with the OPPOSITE sign to a static gradient

====================================================================================================
Part 2  no B = 0 FRW solution with matter in g only (symbolic, from the minisuperspace Lagrangian)
====================================================================================================
  E_N  on the symmetric ansatz: -2*Omega3 + a02*sigma_s*(a(t)**2)**(3/2)*F(0) + 2*beta*(3*Hs**2 - Lambda)*a(t)**3
  E_Nh on the symmetric ansatz: a02*sigma_s*(a(t)**2)**(3/2)*F(0) + 2*gamma*(3*Hs**2 - Lambdah)*a(t)**3
  (Hubble rate common Hs; both equations contain only F(0) through the sqrt(N Nh) prefactor, since dQ/dN = dQ/dNh = 0 at B = 0)
  H^2 from E_N = [Lambda/3 + Omega3/(3*asym**3*beta) - a02*sigma_s*F(0)/(6*beta)];  H^2 from E_Nh = [Lambdah/3 - a02*sigma_s*F(0)/(6*gamma)]
  difference of the two Friedmann relations: Lambda/3 - Lambdah/3 + Omega3/(3*asym**3*beta) + a02*sigma_s*F(0)/(6*gamma) - a02*sigma_s*F(0)/(6*beta)
  ... at beta = gamma: Lambda/3 - Lambdah/3 + Omega3/(3*asym**3*beta)
  [PASS] (control) Part 2: with matter (Omega3 != 0) in g only, the two constraints cannot both hold on the symmetric branch B = 0 for all a: their difference is the dust term Omega3/a^3 (plus beta(Lambda - Lambdah)), which is not a constant   (difference at Lambda = Lambdah: Omega3/(3*asym**3*beta))

